<p>The Javan cucumber, <em>Alsomitra macrocarpa</em>, broadcasts its seeds on papery wings that can glide long distances. Some have been found on the decks of ships.</p>
<p>The unique design inspired aviation pioneer Igo Etrich to build an artificial flying wing, which he adapted into Germany&#8217;s first mass-produced military aeroplane.</p>
